  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-30 on dev 795862a9fc. The defect reproduces EXACTLY as filed; the prescribed fix shape has a verdict-level consequence it does not mention.\n\nREPRO (one file: String k = System.getenv(\"API_KEY\"); System.out.println(k);). hypergumbo survey edges:\n  calls           Main.main -> java:external:0-0:println:external_symbol   {call_construct: method, evidence_type: ast_call_direct}\n  module_attr_ref Main.main -> java:System:0-0:System.out:external_symbol\nverify-claims host_secret -> logging: confirmed_with_caveats, caveat unknown_receiver_scope {entries: [println], method_calls: 1, sites: 1} -- the 1-of-1 untyped site IS the System.out call. No java.io.PrintStream / PrintWriter row exists in java.yaml (the only mention is an ambiguous_names comment), so \"a PrintStream row could never match\" is still hypothetical-but-true.\n\nTHE FIX SHAPE NEEDS A COMPANION, OR IT TRADES A CAVEAT FOR INCONCLUSIVE. Typing the receiver as java.io.PrintStream moves every System.out/err call out of the untyped-receiver caveat and INTO a call on a typed module. java.yaml grants NO module_completeness (0 entries), and a call into an un-enumerated typed java module withholds the verdict: measured, System.out.println(\"starting\") + k.length() reads HS-LOG INCONCLUSIVE, \"calls into 1 module(s) that the I/O catalog could not classify (java.lang.String)\". So shipping this fix alone would turn every java repo that prints from confirmed_with_caveats into inconclusive on each claim whose coverage gate asks for java.io.PrintStream -- unless java.io.PrintStream gets its rows (print/println/printf/format/write/append -> logging, consistent with WI-runos) and a module_completeness decision in the same change. Measure it on the cohort (cassandra / jenkins / sherpa-onnx carried the 09-26 census) before and after, both directions.\n\nORDER: WI-runos first (it settles what System.out IS: logging). Not setting isbefore -- surfaced here only.\nThe census numbers (cassandra 383, jenkins 125, sherpa-onnx 186) are from 09-26 and were NOT re-measured today."  # f4b0
